Hi everyone,

I want to recap what we covered in our meeting yesterday.

1. Please submit a detailed outline of your thesis to me by *Monday March
2nd*. This should include chapters, subheadings, main points you're making
in each section. It's helpful to include how many pages you are planning to
write for each chapter and section.

2. I am able to read one complete, near-final chapter of your thesis, as
long as you send it to me *before March 15.*

3. You are also responsible for sending a different complete near-final
chapter to one of your peers, and reviewing a chapter from one of your
peers and providing feedback. You must send your chapter *before March 15*,
and *return comments also before March 21st*. I will assign reviewers for
everyone.

4. Thesis *Jury Week is April 13-17*; you have to schedule the time with me
and your reader. Details are in the thesis guidelines document.

5. A few of you have asked if other people can attend the thesis jury -- I
don't know but I'll find out.

6. Please continue to send me *status reports weekly*. I had
originally said they were due Mondays, but I don't actually care when they
come as long as you send them every week (so I guess that means Friday is
the deadline). I'm keeping track -- so far I only have one in for this week
(ending tomorrow, 1/23)! Please find a rhythm that works, set a calendar
event for yourself, whatever you need to do!

 7. I am available to meet with you as needed, but you need to request
those check-ins. I would like everyone to meet with me *at least once in
February,* so please email me to schedule.

Let me know if you have any questions or anything!

Dory


